<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shane O'Neill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1530–1567</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shane O'Neill was an Irish chief of the O'Neills of Tyrone in Ulster. Rejecting his father's English earldom, he claimed the traditional title of The O'Neill and dominated Ulster in the 1560s, visiting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1562. He fought both the English and the rival O'Donnells, and after defeat by the O'Donnells in 1567 he was killed by MacDonnell Scots.</p></div>
